### Summary
As a member, I want one consistent way to filter topic lists, in Favoris and in a category, so that I find what I follow from any screen. Operator feedback after a device test, 2026-11-07. **M4**.

### Report
- **Issue 3.** In Favoris ("favoris uniquement", or "favoris & drapeaux" per the settings), tapping a **category title** should open that category **with the same filter applied** (favourites only, or favourites and flags).
- **Issue 4.** Inside a category, there should be a way to filter its topics, consistent with issue 3. Filter by what the rows show as icons or states:
  - favourite (yellow star);
  - flags (blue, red, and other kinds);
  - read or unread (the dot);
  - "participé";
  - anything else HFR offers.

### To analyse (read-only, before any fix)
- What the legacy app does @ 2440d79:
  - the category header tap in Favoris;
  - per-category filters (`owntopic=` values);
  - the Favoris / Suivis / Lus filter.
- What HFR exposes: `forum1f.php?owntopic=1|2|3…`. Cite HFR-PROTOCOL.md or the captures, and list any value that has no capture: never guess.
- Overlap:
  - **#427**: restore the legacy Catégories list, plus the Tous / Favoris / Suivis / Lus filter (UXD-05, 06);
  - the favourites options (LOT-124, #215, done);
  - #584 (row cues).

  Decide whether this extends #427 or stands alone.
